<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Text Content Tags in HTML</title>
</head>
<body>

    <!-- Headings -->
    <h1>My University: Bayero University Kano</h1>
    <h2>Faculty of Computing</h2>
    <h3>Course Title: Web Programming Fundamentals</h3>
    <h4>Topic: HTML Text Formatting</h4>
    <h5>Student Class: IT Siwes 2025</h5>
    <h6>Instructor: Mr. Nibrasudeen Kamal</h6>

    <hr>

    <!-- Paragraph -->
    <p>My favorite topic is <b>web design</b> because it allows me to build 
        <i>creative and interactive</i> websites. 
        I, <u>Ahmad Rabiu</u>, enjoy exploring how design and coding come together to form the web we use every day.</p>

    <!-- Strong & Emphasized text -->
    <p>It is <strong>very important</strong> to understand the structure of a webpage. 
    You should <em>practice writing HTML daily</em> to master it quickly.</p>

    <!-- Marked, Small, Deleted, and Inserted text -->
    <p>Today's lesson focuses on <mark>HTML text formatting tags</mark>.</p>
    <p><small>Tip: Always use indentation to make your code neat and readable.</small></p>
    <p>We no longer use <del>old HTML styling like &lt;font&gt;</del> 
       but prefer <ins>modern CSS styling</ins> for better design control.</p>

    <!-- Subscript and Superscript -->
    <p>Chemical formula for water: H<sub>2</sub>O</p>
    <p>Mathematical formula: a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> = c<sup>2</sup></p>

    <!-- Blockquote and Quote -->
    <blockquote>"The future belongs to those who prepare for it today." – Malcolm X</blockquote>
    <p>As they often say, <q>knowledge is power</q>.</p>

    <!-- Abbreviation and Citation -->
    <p>I am currently learning <abbr title="Cascading Style Sheets">CSS</abbr> and 
       <abbr title="JavaScript">JS</abbr> alongside HTML to enhance my web skills.</p>
    <p>This statement was inspired by <cite>Malcolm X’s Educational Speech</cite>.</p>

    <!-- Code and Preformatted text -->
    <p>Example of code snippet:</p>
    <code>console.log("Welcome to Web Development!");</code>

    <p>Example of preformatted text (short poem):</p>
    <pre>
Code by day,
Dream by night,
Building websites
That shine so bright.
    </pre>

</body>
</html>
